       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that, and I'll add a note to the order recording the confirmation."
