       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Metformin 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. Normal kidney function doesn't make that dose safe, and nothing in the patient details you gave would justify it. The main risks are severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- A lower dose that you choose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily\n- A dose you've reviewed with pharmacy, with a note on the order recording that review\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically necessary, please talk to the pharmacist or attending first. Once you have their sign-off, tell me and I'll reconsider."
